From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jayden Milne <linux@jayd.ml>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 16:34:31 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] iio: qcom_smgr: give the gyroscope and magnetometer a
 rotation matrix

All 3-axis sensors share one mount matrix, [0, -1, 0; -1, 0, 0; 0, 0, 1].
SMGR reports them in north-east-down coordinates, X towards the top of
the screen, Y to its right and Z into it. The rotation into the usual
device frame (X right, Y top, Z out of the screen) is
[0, 1, 0; 1, 0, 0; 0, 0, -1], the example in the ABI documentation. The
shared matrix is its negation, which is not a rotation and flips the
sign of every axis.

That suits the accelerometer: SMGR reports +1 g upwards at rest, and
iio-sensor-proxy takes a negative Y as the upright orientation. For the
gyroscope and the magnetometer it inverts every reading: with the shared
matrix, a compass heading from the magnetometer pointed south when the
device pointed north, and a counter-clockwise turn of the device lying
face up gave a negative angular velocity around Z.

Keep the shared matrix for the accelerometer and give the gyroscope and
the magnetometer the rotation.

Tested on a Galaxy Tab S3 (SM-T820) lying flat, with the shared matrix:
a heading from the magnetometer's X and Y read 180 degrees when a phone
compass said north and 270 at east, and counter-clockwise turns read
about -0.6 rad/s on the gyroscope's Z. The rotation negates both, so
north reads 0, east 90 and the turn is positive. With this patch
in_mount_matrix reads the rotation for both, and iio-sensor-proxy still
reports the upright orientation.

Signed-off-by: Jayden Milne <linux@jayd.ml>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 drivers/iio/common/qcom_smgr/qcom_smgr.c | 23 ++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 22 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/iio/common/qcom_smgr/qcom_smgr.c b/drivers/iio/common/qcom_smgr/qcom_smgr.c
index b08bbc8974c5..0fb476f150dc 100644
--- a/drivers/iio/common/qcom_smgr/qcom_smgr.c
+++ b/drivers/iio/common/qcom_smgr/qcom_smgr.c
@@ -370,8 +370,26 @@ static const struct iio_buffer_setup_ops qcom_smgr_buffer_ops = {
 	.predisable = &qcom_smgr_sensor_predisable
 };
 
-/* SMGR reports values for 3-axis sensors in north-east-down coordinates */
+/*
+ * SMGR reports values for 3-axis sensors in north-east-down coordinates:
+ * X towards the top of the screen, Y towards its right side and Z into it.
+ * This rotation turns them into the usual device frame: X right, Y top,
+ * Z out of the screen.
+ */
 static const struct iio_mount_matrix qcom_smgr_iio_mount_matrix = {
+	.rotation = {
+		"0", "1", "0",
+		"1", "0", "0",
+		"0", "0", "-1"
+	}
+};
+
+/*
+ * SMGR reports the acceleration that holds the device against gravity,
+ * +1 g upwards at rest, while iio-sensor-proxy takes a negative Y as the
+ * upright orientation. The accelerometer's matrix also flips the sign.
+ */
+static const struct iio_mount_matrix qcom_smgr_iio_accel_mount_matrix = {
 	.rotation = {
 		"0", "-1", "0",
 		"-1", "0", "0",
@@ -383,6 +401,9 @@ static const struct iio_mount_matrix *
 qcom_smgr_iio_get_mount_matrix(const struct iio_dev *iio_dev,
 			       const struct iio_chan_spec *chan)
 {
+	if (chan->type == IIO_ACCEL)
+		return &qcom_smgr_iio_accel_mount_matrix;
+
 	return &qcom_smgr_iio_mount_matrix;
 }
 
